# Command-line arguments passed to the prometheus-tplink-plug-exporter server process.
# These arguments configure the exporter's behavior at startup.
#
# Note: Due to shell escaping rules:
#   - In a standard shell string, to pass a backslash to the application (e.g. for regex),
#     you must write two backslashes (e.g., '\\d' for regex '\d').
#   - If this template is rendered by systemd (or systemd's generator), it may apply an
#     additional layer of escaping, requiring you to double the backslashes again
#     (e.g., '\\\\d' to mean regex '\d').
#   - Newlines in the argument string should also be escaped if necessary for the target shell.
#
# Schema field: args (string)
# Default: '' (empty string)
ARGS="{{ args | default('') }}"